From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alina sireneva <alina@tei.su>
Date: Fri, 30 May 2026 14:00:00 +0400
Subject: randomize TLS ClientHello fingerprint per connection to defeat JA3/JA4 DPI

Adds per-connection TLS fingerprint randomization for MTProxy fake-TLS
connections. Rotates between Chrome 120 and Firefox 121 profiles, shuffles
cipher suites and extensions within each profile, inserts RFC 8701 GREASE
values for Chrome profiles, and fragments the ClientHello across multiple
TCP segments to defeat single-packet JA4 fingerprinting.

Based on tdesktop PR #30738 and research into TSPU/ASBI DPI systems that
classify Telegram traffic via its static JA4 fingerprint t13d1516h2_8daaf6152771_d8a2da3f94cd.

